{"id":"costed-provisions","title":"Premiums the Controller priced in its cost letters","question":"When the Board adopted each agreement, what did the Controller say its premium and allowance provisions would add?","finding":"124 premium, allowance or differential lines priced across 33 distinct Controller cost letters; 39 are for fire, police or sheriff units. Largest: Retention Pay (San Francisco Police Officers Association, $9.9 million in the last year); Peace Officers Standards Trainings (POST) Rank Premium (San Francisco Police Officers' Association, $6.6 million in the last year); Training and Education (San Francisco Fire Fighters Union Local 798, $6.0 million in the last year).","how":"Each Controller cost letter attached to an agreement file is read once (duplicates removed by content). Under each union heading, lines that are not wages, fringe or totals and whose label names a premium, pay, allowance, differential or equipment are kept; first and last are the first and last year columns of the letter.","limits":"These are the added costs of changes in that agreement, not the full cost of a premium that already existed. Some letters print their year columns inconsistently (the 2026 police and fire letter labels its union tables FY 2024-25 onward while its combined table starts in FY 2026-27); the columns are taken in printed order. Letters on scanned pages without text are missed.","tier":"OFFICIAL","columns":[{"k":"item","t":"Provision","type":"text"},{"k":"union","t":"Union (as the letter names it)","type":"text"},{"k":"first","t":"Added cost, first year","type":"usd"},{"k":"last","t":"Added cost, last year","type":"usd"},{"k":"year","t":"Letter year","type":"year"},{"k":"link","t":"Cost letter","type":"link"}],"rows":[{"item":"Retention Pay","union":"San Francisco Police Officers Association","first":0.0,"last":9910000.0,"year":2026,"link":{"t":"Board file 260355","u":"https://sfgov.legistar.com/View.ashx?M=F&ID=15399786&GUID=037C4641-9D5E-4D43-9015-08C